          "declaration": {
            "id": "ArithmeticFunction.vonMangoldt"
          },
          "snippet": {
            "text": "/--\nThe `vonMangoldt` function is the function on natural numbers that returns `log p` if the input can\nbe expressed as `p^k` for a prime `p`.\nIn the case when `n` is a prime power, `Nat.minFac` will give the appropriate prime, as it is the\nsmallest prime factor.\n\nIn the `ArithmeticFunction` locale, we have the notation `Λ` for this function.\nThis is also available in the `ArithmeticFunction.vonMangoldt` locale, allowing for selective\naccess to the notation.\n-/\nnoncomputable def vonMangoldt : ArithmeticFunction ℝ :=\n  ⟨fun n => if IsPrimePow n then Real.log (minFac n) else 0, ite_eq_right not_isPrimePow_zero⟩",
            "line": 56,
            "truncated": false
          },
          "proof_context": {
            "declaration": "ArithmeticFunction.vonMangoldt",
            "lines": [
              56,
              67
            ],
            "conclusion": "`Λ n = log (minFac n)` if `n` is a prime power, else `0`: `log p` for `n = p^α`, `α ≥ 1`."
          },
          "destination": {
